# 331. Phase 06F Final Architectural Rules

The following rules are mandatory:

### Rule 1
Frontend is a client, not a domain authority.

### Rule 2
Server state is cached, never owned canonically by the browser.

### Rule 3
UI state remains local unless genuinely global.

### Rule 4
Streaming state is transient delivery/execution state.

### Rule 5
SSE never replaces canonical API reads.

### Rule 6
Long-running operations are backend-owned.

### Rule 7
AI progress must be truthful.

### Rule 8
AI output is untrusted until backend validation and QA.

### Rule 9
Every consequential mutation requires backend confirmation.

### Rule 10
Expensive operations require duplicate protection.

### Rule 11
Stale responses cannot overwrite newer state.

### Rule 12
Event ordering and deduplication must be handled.

### Rule 13
Reconnect must lead to reconciliation.

### Rule 14
Errors must be contextual and recoverable where possible.

### Rule 15
Existing valid state should be preserved during refresh/failure.

### Rule 16
Frontend permission checks are UX only.

### Rule 17
Secrets never enter the frontend.

### Rule 18
No direct database/provider/RAG access.

### Rule 19
Project Definition and Project Instance remain isolated.

### Rule 20
All asynchronous workflows have explicit state machines.

### Rule 21
Unknown backend events/statuses fail safely.

### Rule 22
Logout/account switching clears private state.

### Rule 23
Search and notifications remain authorization-aware.

### Rule 24
Accessibility and responsive behavior are part of runtime behavior.

### Rule 25
Behavioral infrastructure is reused across pages.

